From 9cc0fedf6478b0ca3b25ee68a7d3664ee21998f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: goshoryuken <182185315+goshoryuken@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:24:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Generate 3D CLBs: logic blocks split across layers

A CLB tile can now span layers, with its FLEs (instance_layer_offsets)
and pins (pin_layer) on chosen layers and crossings inside the CLB
charged per layer (layer_crossing_delay). With clb_3d.split_layers in a
setup file, LaZagna cuts each job CLB into one Verilog module per layer
(lazagna/split_clb_layers.py, into task_<benchmark>/clb_layers) and
gives layer crossbars OpenFPGA crossbar mux type in the job copy of the
settings. The VTR and OpenFPGA changes are in patches/3d_clb, applied by
scripts/apply_3d_clb.sh; docs/3d_clb.md explains the attributes. Both
example setups (10 LUTs 5+5, 20 LUTs 10+10 with layer-local pins)
reproduce the split RTL that was laid out and verified.
